.TH mbm_makeimagelist 1 "7 September 2026" "MB-System 5.0" "MB-System 5.0"
.SH NAME
\fBmbm_makeimagelist\fP \- Generate an MB-System stereo imagelist file from a MBARI Low Altitude Survey System (LASS) camera data directory.

.SH VERSION
Version 5.0

.SH SYNOPSIS
mbm_makeimagelist [\fB\-\-help\fP \fB\-\-check\-bayer\fP \fB\-\-imdir=\fP\fIpath2images\fP
\fB\-\-imformat=\fP\fIimage_format\fP \fB\-\-outfile=\fP\fIoutfname\fP
\fB\-\-gpsfile=\fP\fIgpsfname\fP \fB\-\-nogpsfile\fP \fB\-\-nogains\fP]

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBMbm_makeimagelist\fP is a Python macro that generates an MB-System stereo
imagelist file from the directory structure and filenames used by the MBARI
Low Altitude Survey System (LASS) stereo seafloor photography system. It
expects to find left camera images in a subdirectory named \fIPROSILICA_L\fP and
right camera images in a subdirectory named \fIPROSILICA_R\fP of the input image
directory, with each image file's basename being an integer image
acquisition timestamp expressed in microseconds since the Unix epoch.
.P
The left and right image time lists are matched into stereo pairs. By
default this matching also uses a separate GPS trigger time log (a CSV file
whose first column is a microsecond epoch trigger time for each stereo
capture, by default named \fIlogfile_gpstime_cam_sync.csv\fP one directory above
the image directory); each left and right image is paired with the closest
GPS trigger time, and left or right images with no corresponding trigger
within a fixed time tolerance are recorded as unmatched. If \fB\-\-nogpsfile\fP is
given, the left and right image time lists are instead matched directly
against each other using the same time tolerance, without reference to any
GPS trigger log.
.P
Unless \fB\-\-nogains\fP is given, \fBmbm_makeimagelist\fP also opens every input
image with the Python Imaging Library and reads its embedded TIFF
\fIImageDescription\fP tag (tag 270), extracting the first two numeric values
found in that tag's text as the camera's gain and exposure settings at the
time the image was captured. If \fB\-\-check\-bayer\fP is given, the word "color"
in each image's filename is first replaced with "bayer" before the file is
opened to read this tag, on the premise that the original raw Bayer-pattern
image (rather than a subsequently color-processed copy) is more likely to
carry the camera gain/exposure metadata; this substitution only affects
which file is opened to read the gain and exposure values; it does not
change which image files are listed in the output imagelist.
.P
The result is written as a single MB-System imagelist file in the \fI.mb\-2\fP
format, with one line per stereo pair (or single, unmatched image) giving
the left image path (or \fBNULL\fP if there is no left image), the right image
path (or \fBNULL\fP), the paired time (twice), and the left and right camera
gain and exposure values (zero if \fB\-\-nogains\fP was used or no metadata could
be read). The first five lines of the data are additionally prefixed with a
"##" comment marker in the output file.

