.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
This "help" flag causes the program to print out a description
of its command line options and then exit immediately.
.TP
.B \-b, \-\-check\-bayer
.br
Reads camera gain and exposure settings from the corresponding raw Bayer
pattern image file rather than from the (possibly color-processed) image file
actually being listed, by substituting "bayer" for "color" in the filename
used only for that metadata lookup. Has no effect if \fB\-\-nogains\fP is also
given.
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-imdir=\fIpath2images\fP
.br
Sets the path to the directory containing the \fIPROSILICA_L\fP and
\fIPROSILICA_R\fP image subdirectories to be listed. The default is the current
directory (\fI./\fP).
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-imformat=\fIimage_format\fP
.br
Intended to set the image file suffix (for example \fItif\fP) searched for in
the \fIPROSILICA_L\fP and \fIPROSILICA_R\fP subdirectories. In the current
implementation this option instead mistakenly overwrites the image directory
path (\fB\-\-imdir\fP) with the supplied value and has no effect on the image
format searched for, which always remains the default, \fItif\fP.
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-outfile=\fIoutfname\fP
.br
Sets the name of the output imagelist file to be written, without the
\fI.mb\-2\fP suffix, which is appended automatically. If \fIoutfname\fP includes a
directory path, the output file is written to that directory; otherwise it
is written to the image directory set by \fB\-\-imdir\fP. The default output
filename is \fIimagelist\fP, producing \fIimagelist.mb\-2\fP.
.TP
.B \-g, \-\-gpsfile=\fIgpsfname\fP
.br
Sets the filename of the GPS trigger time CSV log used to match left and
right images into stereo pairs. The default is
\fI./../logfile_gpstime_cam_sync.csv\fP relative to the image directory (that
is, one directory above \fB\-\-imdir\fP). Has no effect if \fB\-\-nogpsfile\fP is
given.
.TP
.B \-x, \-\-nogpsfile
.br
Matches left and right camera images into stereo pairs directly by comparing
their timestamps, without reading or requiring a GPS trigger time log file.
.TP
.B \-y, \-\-nogains
.br
Skips opening the image files to read embedded camera gain and exposure
metadata; the gain and exposure values written to the output imagelist are
all zero. This significantly speeds up processing of large image sets when
gain/exposure correction is not needed.

